#!/bin/sh
# In LaTeX mode the words inside math, verbatim and listing environments, the
# arguments of commands such as \include and the column spec of tabular are not
# checked, and nothing after them is skipped. A command that starts with the name
# of one of those, but has no argument, skips nothing. The text in a \colorbox is
# checked, so only that, the word after such a command and the final word are
# reported.
DIR="$(dirname "$0")"
HUNSPELL="${HUNSPELL:-$DIR/../src/tools/hunspell}"
LIBTOOL="${LIBTOOL:-$DIR/../libtool}"
CR=$(printf "\r")
expected='qqafterend
qqboxtext
qqcontrol'
out=$($LIBTOOL --mode=execute "$HUNSPELL" -d "$DIR/latexparser" -t -l "$DIR/latexparser.tex" 2>&1 | tr -d "$CR")
if [ "$out" != "$expected" ]; then
    echo "FAIL: latexparser, got:"
    echo "$out"
    exit 1
fi
echo "PASS: latexparser"
exit 0
